EKS Security Question for You 🚨

Did you know that by default, Kubernetes pods inherit the IAM permissions of the worker node?

That means 👇
One vulnerable pod = access to everything the node can access 😬

This is where IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts) becomes critical.

🔹 IRSA allows each pod to assume its own IAM role
🔹 Permissions are scoped at application level, not node level
🔹 Blast radius is dramatically reduced

👉 In real production EKS clusters, IRSA is not an option — it’s a requirement.


